13. MANUAL PORTABLE BACKUP AND SAFE RESTORE (BUILD THIS FIRST)
==================================================
Implement manual encrypted export/import fully OFFLINE before any Google Drive code. Back up ALL linked financial and user configuration data: accounts, transactions, transfers, adjustments, custom and default categories, budgets, goals, allocations, recurrence rules/occurrences, alert-related state where appropriate, preferences, deletions/tombstones and schema metadata.

Export pipeline: consistent Room snapshot (read transaction) → canonical serialization with schema version and record counts → validate → encrypt with user passphrase → write via ACTION_CREATE_DOCUMENT → verify bytes written and report real completion. Ensure file export is portable to another compatible phone.

Import pipeline: select file → verify header/version/size → request passphrase → authenticate/decrypt → validate types/UUIDs/references/record counts → preview affected record counts → choose Replace or Merge → explicit confirmation → database transaction apply → rollback on ANY failure → requery UI and report actual result.

REPLACE: full, atomic replacement without partially deleting existing records. Consider a safety export before replace.
MERGE: UUID-based deduplication, updatedAt/tombstone awareness; preserve referential integrity, show conflicts and allow explicit per-conflict or clear global resolution choice (keep local / use backup / skip). Never silently overwrite divergent records or resurrect deletions.

Tests required: wrong password, tampered ciphertext, corrupted backup, older schema, duplicate merge, interrupted restore, referential failures, no-data case, and full export/import to a fresh local database.

